{
  "id": 97808572,
  "iid": 2851,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "IEEE 802.11: display Partial TSF as microseconds",
  "description": "To save space, the value of Partial TSF is stored shifted to the right\nby 10. When displaying to the user, shift it back to the left by 10 and\ndisplay as microseconds.\n\nBefore:\n\n                Availability Window Information 0\n                    RSTA Availability Information: 0x02649498, Duration: 10.0 ms (100)\n                        .... .... .... .... 1001 0100 1001 1000 = Partial TSF Timer: 0x9498\n\nAfter:\n\n                Availability Window Information 0\n                    RSTA Availability Information: 0x02649498, Partial TSF Timer: 38952960 μs (38040), Duration: 10.0 ms (100)\n                        .... .... .... .... 1001 0100 1001 1000 = Partial TSF Timer: 38952960 μs (38040)\n\nI was wondering if it's ok to use μ here instead of u. I think it looks nicer. But not sure if there is a policy on non-ASCII characters in Wireshark. I can change it to \"us\" if so.",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2021-04-28T13:42:42.243Z",
